<div id="ctl00_contentAreaPlaceHolder_contentMainInner">
<div id="ctl00_contentAreaPlaceHolder_ContentBlock1">
<div id="ContentAreaWrapper" xmlns:cms="urn:Ektron.Cms.Controls">
<div id="shadow">
<div id="siteWrapper">
<div id="mainWrapper">
<div id="mainWrapperInner">
<div id="contentWrapper">
<div id="content">
<div id="contentMain">
<div id="ctl00_contentAreaPlaceHolder_contentMainInner">
<div id="ctl00_contentAreaPlaceHolder_ContentBlock1">
<div id="ContentAreaWrapper" xmlns:cms="urn:Ektron.Cms.Controls">
<div id="shadow">
<div id="siteWrapper">
<div id="mainWrapper">
<div id="mainWrapperInner">
<div id="contentWrapper">
<div id="content">
<div id="contentMain">
<div id="ctl00_contentAreaPlaceHolder_contentMainInner">
<div id="ctl00_contentAreaPlaceHolder_ContentBlock1">
<div id="ContentAreaWrapper" xmlns:cms="urn:Ektron.Cms.Controls">
<p><span data-contrast="auto">Rick Gieser, a community-minded lifelong learner with a deep passion for DuPage County’s forest preserves, brings extensive experience in communications and government to his role on the District’s board of commissioners. Elected in 2024, Gieser is committed to making the forest preserves more accessible by expanding trails, supporting green initiatives, and strengthening the Forest Preserve District’s leadership through scientific research.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">Gieser has a long history of public service, including previously serving for nearly 20 years as a trustee for the Village of Carol Stream. He also serves on the village’s historical society board and remains an active community volunteer.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">Gieser has enjoyed the DuPage forest preserves for many years, but during the pandemic, he and his wife, Kim, set out to visit every preserve with a trail and parking area. He enjoys walking the trails, photographing nature for social media and identifying the plants, trees, bugs, and birds he encounters along the way. One of his favorite spots is Elsen’s Hill at West DuPage Woods in West Chicago, where he loves to observe the blackberries in the prairie change color in the fall.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">Professionally, Gieser serves as the public relations director for Zanies Comedy Clubs and was a former producer for WGN Radio.&nbsp;</span><span data-ccp-props="{}">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">Gieser earned his bachelor’s degree in telecommunications from Indiana University. He and Kim have one adult son, Ricky, a bat biologist with the Illinois Natural History Survey.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}">&nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</form></div>
